    "settings.compass.note": "A small see-through ball floating above the back of your hand that shows the real room as you see it. Only the half facing you is drawn: the part above the real horizon is tinted like the sky, the part below like the ground, with a bright line on the real horizon between them. The glowing dot is real down (gravity); when down is on the far side of the ball it shows as a dimmer ring, and the small glowing triangle just outside the edge always points toward real down. When 3-axis rotation tilts the world, the ball keeps showing the real floor. It is a SteamVR overlay: it takes no input and does not affect VRChat's controls or picture. \"While flying\" shows it while flight is ON; \"Always\" whenever FlugelKranz is connected to SteamVR (for example with flight OFF and Drag on).",
